# Typography

## Source of Truth

Design Tokens are the source of truth. Flutter typography must match tokens.

## English Typography

- Sizes: `TypeScale` (title1=48, title2=32, title3=24, large=18, regular=16, small=14, tiny=12)
- Line heights: `TypeScale.lineHeight*` constants
- Letter spacing (titles only): `TypeScale.trackingTitle1` (-0.96), `trackingTitle2` (-0.32), `trackingTitle3` (-0.12)
- Weights: `AppFont.regular` (w400), `medium` (w500), `semiBold` (w600), `bold` (w700)
- Pre-built styles: `AppFontStyle.*` or `AppFont.<weight>.<scale>` via `AppFontScaleX`

## Arabic Typography

- Same font sizes as English — different line heights from `ArabicTypeScale`
- Never reuse English `TypeScale` line heights for Arabic text
- Pre-built styles: `AppFontArabicStyle.*` or `AppFontArabic.<weight>.<arScale>` via `AppFontArabicScaleX`

## Title Weights

| Style | Weight | Token |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Title 1 | Bold w700 | `AppFont.bold.title1` |
| Title 2 | Bold w700 | `AppFont.bold.title2` |
| Title 3 | SemiBold w600 | `AppFont.semiBold.title3` |
| Body | Regular w400 | `AppFont.regular.*` |

## Widget Layer

Consume via `context.appTypography.*` — never hardcode `fontSize`, `fontWeight`, or `height`.

## Token Gap

`FontWeight.w500` (Medium) is used in Flutter but not yet in design tokens — intentionally kept until tokens add `fontWeights.inter-medium`.

Do not add new `TypeScale` entries without a corresponding design token.
